{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Abstract Factory Pattern.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Abstract Factory Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"abstract factory pattern abstract factory pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Abstract Factory Pattern.md","fileName":"Abstract Factory Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Abstract Factory Pattern","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-21 22:12\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Object-Oriented Design Patterns]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Abstract Factory Pattern.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Abstract Factory Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"abstract factory pattern abstract factory pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Abstract Factory Pattern.md","fileName":"Abstract Factory Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Abstract Factory Pattern","heading":"Abstract Factory Pattern","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"An abstract factory supplies a family of related objects through a common creation contract, leaving the choice of concrete family outside the client. A caller asks for products it can use without coupling itself to the classes that construct them. In the book's inventory-command example, shared command abstractions let the console workflow invoke differently created commands through a common interface, though that example is closer to a general factory than a strict family-of-products abstract factory.\n\nAn abstract factory adds a factory-level abstraction so a client can request related products without selecting a concrete product family or concrete factory directly. The pattern is most valuable when those products must remain compatible as a group.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Abstract Factory Pattern.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Abstract Factory Pattern.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"abstract factory pattern abstract factory pattern","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Abstract Factory Pattern.md","fileName":"Abstract Factory Pattern.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Abstract Factory Pattern","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf]]\n\n[[hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Object-Oriented Design Patterns","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","hands-ondesignpatternswithcandnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}